8350 @4.0 GHz"],["Memory","8 GB RAM DDR3"],["Hard Drive","40 GB free space"],["Graphics","NVIDIA\u00ae GeForce\u00ae GTX 780 / AMD Radeon\u2122 R9 290 (2GB VRAM)"],["DirectX\u00ae","Version 11"],["Sound","DirectX\u00ae compatible"]],"deck":3,"blurb":"Harran, a quarantined city devastated by a viral outbreak, is the setting of Dying Light, a first-person survival game in an open world. The player scavenges for supplies, crafts and repairs melee weapons, and uses parkour-style movement across rooftops to travel and escape. The day-night cycle changes the danger: daytime favors gathering and completing quests, while night brings faster, more aggressive threats.\n\nIt can be played alone or in online co-op, and a PvP mode is available. The Essentials Edition packages the base game with several add-ons, and the free Retouched Update revises the visuals and soundtrack for all owners. It suits players who like survival games built around mobility as much as combat."}}